{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# DemandCast - Phase 2: Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** DataCo SMART SUPPLY CHAIN FOR BIG DATA ANALYSIS\n",
    "**Source:** Mendeley Data, Version 5, DOI: 10.17632/8gx2fvg2k6.5\n",
    "**License:** CC BY 4.0\n",
    "**Citation:** Constante, Fabian; Silva, Fernando; Pereira, Antonio (2019)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook performs comprehensive exploratory data analysis on the processed demand data.\n",
    "All charts include written business interpretations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '../src')\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import yaml\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "import plotly.express as px\n",
    "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
    "from plotly.subplots import make_subplots\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load config\n",
    "with open('../config.yaml', 'r') as f:\n",
    "    config = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "project_root = Path(__file__).parent.parent\n",
    "processed_dir = project_root / config['paths']['processed_data']\n",
    "reports_dir = project_root / config['paths']['reports_dir']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Processed data directory: {processed_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Reports directory: {reports_dir}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load all processed datasets\n",
    "datasets = {}\n",
    "for level in ['overall', 'category', 'market', 'region', 'category_market']:\n",
    "    path = processed_dir / f\"demand_{level}.parquet\"\n",
    "    if path.exists():\n",
    "        datasets[level] = pd.read_parquet(path)\n",
    "        print(f\"Loaded {level}: {datasets[level].shape}\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(f\"Missing: {level}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure date columns are datetime\n",
    "for level, df in datasets.items():\n",
    "    if 'order_week_start' in df.columns:\n",
    "        df['order_week_start'] = pd.to_datetime(df['order_week_start'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Overall Demand Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Overall demand time series\n",
    "overall = datasets['overall'].copy()\n",
    "overall = overall.sort_values('order_week_start')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Weekly demand line chart\n",
    "fig = px.line(overall, x='order_week_start', y='order_item_quantity',\n",
    "              title='Overall Weekly Demand (Order Item Quantity)',\n",
    "              labels={'order_week_start': 'Week', 'order_item_quantity': 'Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Summary statistics\n",
    "print(f\"Total weeks: {len(overall)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Date range: {overall['order_week_start'].min()} to {overall['order_week_start'].max()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total units sold: {overall['order_item_quantity'].sum():,.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean weekly demand: {overall['order_item_quantity'].mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Std weekly demand: {overall['order_item_quantity'].std():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min weekly demand: {overall['order_item_quantity'].min():.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max weekly demand: {overall['order_item_quantity'].max():.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Coefficient of variation: {overall['order_item_quantity'].std()/overall['order_item_quantity'].mean():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** The overall weekly demand shows the aggregate sales pattern across all categories and markets. The coefficient of variation indicates the relative volatility of demand. A CV > 0.5 suggests high variability, which impacts safety stock requirements and forecast accuracy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Monthly aggregation\n",
    "overall_monthly = overall.set_index('order_week_start').resample('MS')['order_item_quantity'].sum().reset_index()\n",
    "overall_monthly.columns = ['month', 'quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(overall_monthly, x='month', y='quantity',\n",
    "             title='Overall Monthly Demand',\n",
    "             labels={'month': 'Month', 'quantity': 'Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quarterly aggregation\n",
    "overall_quarterly = overall.set_index('order_week_start').resample('Q')['order_item_quantity'].sum().reset_index()\n",
    "overall_quarterly.columns = ['quarter', 'quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(overall_quarterly, x='quarter', y='quantity',\n",
    "             title='Overall Quarterly Demand',\n",
    "             labels={'quarter': 'Quarter', 'quantity': 'Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Monthly and quarterly views smooth out weekly noise and reveal seasonal patterns. Quarterly trends are particularly useful for capacity planning and budgeting. Look for consistent Q4 peaks (holiday season) or Q1 dips (post-holiday)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Category Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category-level analysis\n",
    "cat = datasets['category'].copy()\n",
    "cat['order_week_start'] = pd.to_datetime(cat['order_week_start'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total demand by category\n",
    "cat_totals = cat.groupby('category_id')['order_item_quantity'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).reset_index()\n",
    "cat_totals.columns = ['category_id', 'total_quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(cat_totals.head(20), x='category_id', y='total_quantity',\n",
    "             title='Top 20 Categories by Total Demand',\n",
    "             labels={'category_id': 'Category ID', 'total_quantity': 'Total Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pareto analysis\n",
    "cat_totals['cumulative_pct'] = cat_totals['total_quantity'].cumsum() / cat_totals['total_quantity'].sum() * 100\n",
    "cat_totals['rank'] = range(1, len(cat_totals) + 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.line(cat_totals, x='rank', y='cumulative_pct',\n",
    "              title='Pareto Analysis: Cumulative Demand Share by Category',\n",
    "              labels={'rank': 'Category Rank', 'cumulative_pct': 'Cumulative % of Total Demand'})\n",
    "fig.add_hline(y=80, line_dash='dash', line_color='red', annotation_text='80% threshold')\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Top categories contributing to 80% of demand\n",
    "top_80 = cat_totals[cat_totals['cumulative_pct'] <= 80]\n",
    "print(f\"Categories for 80% of demand: {len(top_80)} out of {len(cat_totals)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Top categories: {top_80['category_id'].tolist()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** The Pareto analysis reveals demand concentration. If few categories drive 80% of demand (typical 80/20 rule), forecasting efforts should prioritize these high-volume categories. Categories with very low or sporadic demand may need different modeling approaches (e.g., intermittent demand models)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category demand over time - top 10 categories\n",
    "top_10_cats = cat_totals.head(10)['category_id'].tolist()\n",
    "cat_top = cat[cat['category_id'].isin(top_10_cats)]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.line(cat_top, x='order_week_start', y='order_item_quantity', color='category_id',\n",
    "              title='Weekly Demand by Top 10 Categories',\n",
    "              labels={'order_week_start': 'Week', 'order_item_quantity': 'Units Sold', 'category_id': 'Category'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=500, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category demand statistics\n",
    "cat_stats = cat.groupby('category_id')['order_item_quantity'].agg([\n",
    "    'count', 'sum', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max'\n",
    "]).round(2).reset_index()\n",
    "cat_stats.columns = ['category_id', 'weeks', 'total', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max']\n",
    "cat_stats['cv'] = (cat_stats['std'] / cat_stats['mean']).round(3)\n",
    "cat_stats = cat_stats.sort_values('total', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(cat_stats.head(15).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Categories with constant demand (std = 0)\n",
    "constant_cats = cat_stats[cat_stats['std'] == 0]\n",
    print(f\"Categories with constant demand (std=0): {len(constant_cats)}\")\n",
    "print(constant_cats[['category_id', 'mean', 'weeks']].to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Categories with constant demand (std=0) are likely single-unit products with consistent ordering patterns. These are easy to forecast but may represent niche products. High CV categories have volatile demand and require more safety stock. The number of weeks with data indicates series length - categories with fewer than 52 weeks may not have full yearly seasonality captured."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Market Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Market-level analysis\n",
    "mkt = datasets['market'].copy()\n",
    "mkt['order_week_start'] = pd.to_datetime(mkt['order_week_start'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total demand by market\n",
    "mkt_totals = mkt.groupby('market')['order_item_quantity'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).reset_index()\n",
    "mkt_totals.columns = ['market', 'total_quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(mkt_totals, x='market', y='total_quantity',\n",
    "             title='Total Demand by Market',\n",
    "             labels={'market': 'Market', 'total_quantity': 'Total Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Market demand over time\n",
    "fig = px.line(mkt, x='order_week_start', y='order_item_quantity', color='market',\n",
    "              title='Weekly Demand by Market',\n",
    "              labels={'order_week_start': 'Week', 'order_item_quantity': 'Units Sold', 'market': 'Market'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=500, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Market-level demand shows geographic distribution of sales. Markets with growing trends represent expansion opportunities. Markets with declining trends may need investigation. Seasonal patterns may differ by market (e.g., Southern vs Northern hemisphere seasons)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Market statistics\n",
    "mkt_stats = mkt.groupby('market')['order_item_quantity'].agg([\n",
    "    'count', 'sum', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max'\n",
    "]).round(2).reset_index()\n",
    "mkt_stats.columns = ['market', 'weeks', 'total', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max']\n",
    "mkt_stats['cv'] = (mkt_stats['std'] / mkt_stats['mean']).round(3)\n",
    "print(mkt_stats.to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Region Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Region-level analysis\n",
    "reg = datasets['region'].copy()\n",
    "reg['order_week_start'] = pd.to_datetime(reg['order_week_start'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total demand by region (top 15)\n",
    "reg_totals = reg.groupby('order_region')['order_item_quantity'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False).reset_index()\n",
    "reg_totals.columns = ['order_region', 'total_quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(reg_totals.head(15), x='order_region', y='total_quantity',\n",
    "             title='Top 15 Regions by Total Demand',\n",
    "             labels={'order_region': 'Region', 'total_quantity': 'Total Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Region demand over time (top 10)\n",
    "top_10_reg = reg_totals.head(10)['order_region'].tolist()\n",
    "reg_top = reg[reg['order_region'].isin(top_10_reg)]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.line(reg_top, x='order_week_start', y='order_item_quantity', color='order_region',\n",
    "              title='Weekly Demand by Top 10 Regions',\n",
    "              labels={'order_week_start': 'Week', 'order_item_quantity': 'Units Sold', 'order_region': 'Region'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=500, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Regional analysis reveals sub-market performance within larger markets. High-performing regions may warrant dedicated inventory or marketing. Regions with sparse data (few weeks) need caution in forecasting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Region statistics\n",
    "reg_stats = reg.groupby('order_region')['order_item_quantity'].agg([\n",
    "    'count', 'sum', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max'\n",
    "]).round(2).reset_index()\n",
    "reg_stats.columns = ['order_region', 'weeks', 'total', 'mean', 'median', 'std', 'min', 'max']\n",
    "reg_stats['cv'] = (reg_stats['std'] / reg_stats['mean']).round(3)\n",
    "reg_stats = reg_stats.sort_values('total', ascending=False)\n",
    "print(reg_stats.head(15).to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Category x Market Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category-Market combination analysis\n",
    "cm = datasets['category_market'].copy()\n",
    "cm['order_week_start'] = pd.to_datetime(cm['order_week_start'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Total demand by category-market\n",
    "cm_totals = cm.groupby(['category_id', 'market'])['order_item_quantity'].sum().reset_index()\n",
    "cm_totals = cm_totals.sort_values('order_item_quantity', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Top 20 combinations\n",
    "fig = px.bar(cm_totals.head(20), x='category_id', y='order_item_quantity', color='market',\n",
    "             title='Top 20 Category-Market Combinations by Demand',\n",
    "             labels={'category_id': 'Category ID', 'order_item_quantity': 'Total Units Sold', 'market': 'Market'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Category-market combinations identify which product categories perform best in which markets. This guides localized inventory planning and marketing. Combinations with sufficient data (>52 weeks) can support individual forecasting models; sparse combinations may need pooling or hierarchical approaches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Data sufficiency for category-market combinations\n",
    "cm_counts = cm.groupby(['category_id', 'market']).size().reset_index(name='weeks')\n",
    "cm_counts = cm_counts.sort_values('weeks', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total combinations: {len(cm_counts)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Combinations with >=52 weeks: {(cm_counts['weeks'] >= 52).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Combinations with >=26 weeks: {(cm_counts['weeks'] >= 26).sum()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Combinations with <26 weeks: {(cm_counts['weeks'] < 26).sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.histogram(cm_counts, x='weeks', nbins=30,\n",
    "                   title='Distribution of Weeks of Data per Category-Market Combination',\n",
    "                   labels={'weeks': 'Number of Weeks with Data', 'count': 'Number of Combinations'})\n",
    "fig.add_vline(x=26, line_dash='dash', line_color='red', annotation_text='Min 26 weeks')\n",
    "fig.add_vline(x=52, line_dash='dash', line_color='orange', annotation_text='Full year (52 weeks)')\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Distribution Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Overall demand distribution\n",
    "fig = px.histogram(overall, x='order_item_quantity', nbins=30,\n",
    "                   title='Distribution of Weekly Demand (Overall)',\n",
    "                   labels={'order_item_quantity': 'Weekly Units Sold', 'count': 'Frequency'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Box plot\n",
    "fig = px.box(overall, y='order_item_quantity',\n",
    "             title='Weekly Demand Box Plot (Overall)',\n",
    "             labels={'order_item_quantity': 'Weekly Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Summary statistics\n",
    "print(overall['order_item_quantity'].describe(percentiles=[0.01, 0.05, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.95, 0.99]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** The demand distribution shows central tendency and spread. Right-skewed distributions are common in demand data. Outliers (beyond 1.5*IQR) represent unusual spikes that may be promotions, stockouts, or data errors. Understanding the distribution helps choose appropriate forecasting models and safety stock calculations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category-level demand distributions\n",
    "cat_dist = cat.groupby('category_id')['order_item_quantity'].agg(['mean', 'std', 'median']).reset_index()\n",
    "cat_dist['cv'] = cat_dist['std'] / cat_dist['mean']\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.scatter(cat_dist, x='mean', y='cv', hover_data=['category_id'],\n",
    "                 title='Category Demand: Mean vs Coefficient of Variation',\n",
    "                 labels={'mean': 'Mean Weekly Demand', 'cv': 'Coefficient of Variation (CV)'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Gini coefficient for demand concentration\n",
    "def gini_coefficient(x):\n",
    "    x = np.array(x)\n",
    "    if np.all(x == 0):\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    x = np.sort(x)\n",
    "    n = len(x)\n",
    "    index = np.arange(1, n + 1)\n",
    "    return (2 * np.sum(index * x) / (n * np.sum(x))) - (n + 1) / n\n",
    "\n",
    "overall_gini = gini_coefficient(cat_totals['total_quantity'].values)\n",
    "print(f\"Gini coefficient (category demand concentration): {overall_gini:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Market Gini\n",
    "mkt_gini = gini_coefficient(mkt_totals['total_quantity'].values)\n",
    "print(f\"Gini coefficient (market demand concentration): {mkt_gini:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** The Mean-CV plot segments categories by demand pattern: high mean/low CV = stable high-volume (easy to forecast), low mean/high CV = erratic low-volume (hard to forecast, consider intermittent models). Gini coefficient measures inequality: 0 = perfectly even, 1 = completely concentrated. High Gini means few categories/markets dominate demand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Growth and Decline Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Year-over-year growth\n",
    "overall['year'] = overall['order_week_start'].dt.year\n",
    "overall['week_of_year'] = overall['order_week_start'].dt.isocalendar().week\n",
    "\n",
    "yearly = overall.groupby('year')['order_item_quantity'].sum().reset_index()\n",
    "yearly.columns = ['year', 'total_quantity']\n",
    "yearly['yoy_growth'] = yearly['total_quantity'].pct_change() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(yearly, x='year', y='total_quantity',\n",
    "             title='Annual Demand with YoY Growth %',\n",
    "             labels={'year': 'Year', 'total_quantity': 'Total Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.add_scatter(x=yearly['year'], y=yearly['yoy_growth'], mode='lines+markers',\n",
    "                name='YoY Growth %', yaxis='y2', line_color='red')\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    yaxis=dict(title='Total Units Sold'),\n",
    "    yaxis2=dict(title='YoY Growth %', overlaying='y', side='right'),\n",
    "    height=400, template='plotly_white'\n",
    ")\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(yearly.to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Year-over-year growth reveals business trajectory. Positive growth suggests expanding demand requiring capacity increases. Negative growth may indicate market saturation or competitive pressure. The weekly granularity allows detection of trend changes within years."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Category-level growth trends\n",
    "cat_yearly = cat.groupby(['category_id', cat['order_week_start'].dt.year])['order_item_quantity'].sum().reset_index()\n",
    "cat_yearly.columns = ['category_id', 'year', 'total_quantity']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute YoY growth for categories with at least 2 years of data\n",
    "cat_growth = cat_yearly.groupby('category_id').apply(lambda g: g.sort_values('year').assign(yoy_growth=g['total_quantity'].pct_change() * 100)).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Latest year growth by category (for categories with 2017 data)\n",
    "latest_growth = cat_growth[cat_growth['year'] == 2017].sort_values('yoy_growth', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(latest_growth.head(15), x='category_id', y='yoy_growth',\n",
    "             title='Top 15 Categories by YoY Growth (2017 vs 2016)',\n",
    "             labels={'category_id': 'Category ID', 'yoy_growth': 'YoY Growth %'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(latest_growth.tail(15), x='category_id', y='yoy_growth',\n",
    "             title='Bottom 15 Categories by YoY Growth (2017 vs 2016)',\n",
    "             labels={'category_id': 'Category ID', 'yoy_growth': 'YoY Growth %'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Category-level growth identifies winners and losers. Growing categories need capacity planning; declining categories may need promotional support or phase-out planning. Categories with insufficient history (e.g., new products in 2017) cannot have YoY growth computed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Seasonality Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Monthly seasonality heatmap - overall\n",
    "overall['month'] = overall['order_week_start'].dt.month\n",
    "overall['year'] = overall['order_week_start'].dt.year\n",
    "\n",
    "monthly_pivot = overall.pivot_table(index='year', columns='month', values='order_item_quantity', aggfunc='mean')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.imshow(monthly_pivot.values,\n",
    "                x=[f'M{m}' for m in monthly_pivot.columns],\n",
    "                y=monthly_pivot.index.astype(str),\n",
    "                color_continuous_scale='RdYlBu_r',\n",
    "                title='Monthly Average Demand Heatmap (Overall)',\n",
    "                labels={'x': 'Month', 'y': 'Year', 'color': 'Avg Weekly Demand'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** The heatmap reveals seasonal patterns across years. Consistent patterns across years (e.g., high demand in Nov-Dec) indicate true seasonality. Patterns that change year-to-year may be trend-driven or event-driven. This informs seasonal model selection (Holt-Winters, SARIMA) and promotional planning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Monthly seasonality by category (top 10)\n",
    "cat['month'] = cat['order_week_start'].dt.month\n",
    "cat['year'] = cat['order_week_start'].dt.year\n",
    "\n",
    "top_10_cats = cat_totals.head(10)['category_id'].tolist()\n",
    "cat_top = cat[cat['category_id'].isin(top_10_cats)]\n",
    "\n",
    "cat_monthly = cat_top.pivot_table(index=['category_id', 'year'], columns='month', values='order_item_quantity', aggfunc='mean')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot for each top category\n",
    "for cat_id in top_10_cats:\n",
    "    cat_data = cat_monthly.loc[cat_id]\n",
    "    fig = px.imshow([cat_data.values],\n",
    "                    x=[f'M{m}' for m in cat_data.index],\n",
    "                    y=[f'{cat_id}'],\n",
    "                    color_continuous_scale='RdYlBu_r',\n",
    "                    title=f'Category {cat_id} Monthly Seasonality',\n",
    "                    labels={'x': 'Month', 'y': 'Year', 'color': 'Avg Weekly Demand'})\n",
    "    fig.update_layout(height=200, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "    fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Weekly seasonality (week of year)\n",
    "overall['week_of_year'] = overall['order_week_start'].dt.isocalendar().week\n",
    "\n",
    "weekly_avg = overall.groupby('week_of_year')['order_item_quantity'].mean().reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.line(weekly_avg, x='week_of_year', y='order_item_quantity',\n",
    "              title='Average Weekly Demand by Week of Year (Overall)',\n",
    "              labels={'week_of_year': 'Week of Year', 'order_item_quantity': 'Avg Units Sold'})\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=400, template='plotly_white')\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Seasonal decomposition using statsmodels\n",
    "from statsmodels.tsa.seasonal import seasonal_decompose\n",
    "\n",
    "ts = overall.set_index('order_week_start')['order_item_quantity'].asfreq('W-MON')\n",
    "decomposition = seasonal_decompose(ts, model='additive', period=52)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = make_subplots(rows=4, cols=1, shared_xaxes=True,\n",
    "                    subplot_titles=('Observed', 'Trend', 'Seasonal', 'Residual'))\n",
    "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=decomposition.observed.index, y=decomposition.observed, name='Observed'), row=1, col=1)\n",
    "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=decomposition.trend.index, y=decomposition.trend, name='Trend'), row=2, col=1)\n",
    "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=decomposition.seasonal.index, y=decomposition.seasonal, name='Seasonal'), row=3, col=1)\n",
    "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=decomposition.resid.index, y=decomposition.resid, name='Residual'), row=4, col=1)\n",
    "fig.update_layout(height=800, template='plotly_white', showlegend=False)\n",
    "fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Business Interpretation:** Seasonal decomposition separates trend, seasonal, and residual components. The trend shows long-term direction. The seasonal component reveals repeating patterns (e.g., holiday peaks). Residuals are the unpredictable remainder. Strong seasonal component (relative to residual) suggests seasonal models will perform well. Weak seasonality suggests simpler models may suffice."
   ]
  },
